docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/tasks/T23.md:12:This task implements the public memory store API: create, read, update, delete, and the state-machine transitions over `VerificationStatus` (`unverified → in_review → verified`, plus `stale`, `contradicted`, `superseded`, `expired`, `invalidated`). Writes are idempotent on a caller-provided idempotency key so retries do not double-insert. Every status transition emits the right event via the T13 writer (`MemoryCreated`, `MemoryUpdated`, `MemoryInvalidated`, `MemoryConsolidated`) and records an evidence row pointing at the triggering event. Without this task, the redesigned schema has no callable API and Phase 4 retrieval has nothing to read.
docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/tasks/T23.md:36:2. Define the create API: `pub fn MemoryStore::create(&self, draft: MemoryDraft, idempotency_key: IdempotencyKey) -> Result<MemoryRecord, MemoryStoreError>`. `MemoryDraft` is `MemoryRecord` minus `memory_id`, `created_at`, `updated_at`, `usefulness_score`, `verification_status` (initial status is always `Unverified`). On insert, emit `MemoryCreated` event with payload `{ memory_id, class, stream, scope, idempotency_key }`. Insert evidence rows from `draft.initial_evidence`.
docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/tasks/T23.md:37:3. Implement idempotency: store `idempotency_key` in a `memory_idempotency` table mapping key → `memory_id`. On `create` with a key that already exists, return the existing record without inserting; never raise an error.
docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/tasks/T23.md:44:5. Define the update API: `pub fn update(&self, memory_id, patch: MemoryPatch, evidence: Option<MemoryEvidence>, idempotency_key: IdempotencyKey) -> Result<MemoryRecord, MemoryStoreError>`. `MemoryPatch` is the set of optional updatable fields (content, confidence, freshness_policy, validity_conditions, invalidation_triggers, scope) but NOT `verification_status` (use `transition_status`) and NOT `memory_id` (immutable). Emit `MemoryUpdated` event.
docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/tasks/T23.md:45:6. Define the delete API: `pub fn delete(&self, memory_id, reason: &str) -> Result<(), MemoryStoreError>`. Delete is soft: set `verification_status = Invalidated` and write a tombstone row; the original record is kept for replay. Emit `MemoryInvalidated` event.
docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/tasks/T23.md:60:8. Every transition writes an evidence row pointing at the triggering event and emits the right lifecycle event: `Verified`/`Stale`/`Contradicted`/`Superseded`/`Expired` use `MemoryUpdated`; `Invalidated` uses `MemoryInvalidated`; `MemoryConsolidated` is reserved for Phase 6 consolidation transitions.
